   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_cryp.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *          functionalities of the  Cryptographic processor (CRYP) peripheral:
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration functions
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *           + Data treatment functions 
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *           + Context swapping functions     
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *           + DMA interface function       
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management       
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** @verbatim
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===================================================================      
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****                  ##### How to use this driver #####
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  =================================================================== 
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..]
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) Enable the CRYP controller clock using 
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        RCC_AHB2PeriphClockCmd(RCC_AHB2Periph_CRYP, ENABLE); function.
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) Initialize the CRYP using CRYP_Init(), CRYP_KeyInit() and if needed 
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        CRYP_IVInit(). 
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) Flush the IN and OUT FIFOs by using CRYP_FIFOFlush() function.
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) Enable the CRYP controller using the CRYP_Cmd() function. 
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) If using DMA for Data input and output transfer, activate the needed DMA 
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc52A741.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        Requests using CRYP_DMACmd() function 
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) If DMA is not used for data transfer, use CRYP_DataIn() and  CRYP_DataOut() 
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        functions to enter data to IN FIFO and get result from OUT FIFO.
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) To control CRYP events you can use one of the following two methods:
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) Check on CRYP flags using the CRYP_GetFlagStatus() function.  
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) Use CRYP interrupts through the function CRYP_ITConfig() at 
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             initialization phase and CRYP_GetITStatus() function into interrupt 
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             routines in processing phase.
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) Save and restore Cryptographic processor context using CRYP_SaveContext() 
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        and CRYP_RestoreContext() functions.     
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *** Procedure to perform an encryption or a decryption ***
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ========================================================== 
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *** Initialization ***
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ====================== 
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] 
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) Initialize the peripheral using CRYP_Init(), CRYP_KeyInit() and CRYP_IVInit 
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        functions:
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) Configure the key size (128-, 192- or 256-bit, in the AES only) 
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) Enter the symmetric key 
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) Configure the data type
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) In case of decryption in AES-ECB or AES-CBC, you must prepare 
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             the key: configure the key preparation mode. Then Enable the CRYP 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             peripheral using CRYP_Cmd() function: the BUSY flag is set. 
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             Wait until BUSY flag is reset : the key is prepared for decryption
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) Configure the algorithm and chaining (the DES/TDES in ECB/CBC, the 
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             AES in ECB/CBC/CTR) 
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) Configure the direction (encryption/decryption).
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) Write the initialization vectors (in CBC or CTR modes only)
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) Flush the IN and OUT FIFOs using the CRYP_FIFOFlush() function
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *** Basic Processing mode (polling mode) *** 
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   ============================================  
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   [..]
  72:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) Enable the cryptographic processor using CRYP_Cmd() function.
  73:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  74:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) Write the first blocks in the input FIFO (2 to 8 words) using 
  75:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****         CRYP_DataIn() function.
  76:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  77:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) Repeat the following sequence until the complete message has been 
  78:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****         processed:
  79:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  80:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****         (++) Wait for flag CRYP_FLAG_OFNE occurs (using CRYP_GetFlagStatus() 
  81:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             function), then read the OUT-FIFO using CRYP_DataOut() function
  82:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             (1 block or until the FIFO is empty)
  83:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  84:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          (++) Wait for flag CRYP_FLAG_IFNF occurs, (using CRYP_GetFlagStatus() 
  85:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             function then write the IN FIFO using CRYP_DataIn() function 
  86:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             (1 block or until the FIFO is full)
  87:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc52A741.s 			page 3


  88:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) At the end of the processing, CRYP_FLAG_BUSY flag will be reset and 
  89:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****           both FIFOs are empty (CRYP_FLAG_IFEM is set and CRYP_FLAG_OFNE is 
  90:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****           reset). You can disable the peripheral using CRYP_Cmd() function.
  91:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  92:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *** Interrupts Processing mode *** 
  93:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ==================================
  94:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] In this mode, Processing is done when the data are transferred by the 
  95:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       CPU during interrupts.
  96:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
  97:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) Enable the interrupts CRYP_IT_INI and CRYP_IT_OUTI using CRYP_ITConfig()
  98:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****         function.
  99:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
 100:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) Enable the cryptographic processor using CRYP_Cmd() function.
 101:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
 102:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) In the CRYP_IT_INI interrupt handler : load the input message into the 
 103:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          IN FIFO using CRYP_DataIn() function . You can load 2 or 4 words at a 
 104:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          time, or load data until the IN FIFO is full. When the last word of
 105:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          the message has been entered into the IN FIFO, disable the CRYP_IT_INI 
 106:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          interrupt (using CRYP_ITConfig() function).
 107:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
 108:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) In the CRYP_IT_OUTI interrupt handler : read the output message from 
 109:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          the OUT FIFO using CRYP_DataOut() function. You can read 1 block (2 or 
 110:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          4 words) at a time or read data until the FIFO is empty.
 111:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          When the last word has been read, INIM=0, BUSY=0 and both FIFOs are 
 112:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          empty (CRYP_FLAG_IFEM is set and CRYP_FLAG_OFNE is reset). 
 113:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          You can disable the CRYP_IT_OUTI interrupt (using CRYP_ITConfig() 
 114:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          function) and you can disable the peripheral using CRYP_Cmd() function.
 115:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
 116:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *** DMA Processing mode *** 
 117:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===========================
 118:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] In this mode, Processing is done when the DMA is used to transfer the 
 119:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       data from/to the memory.
 120:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
 121:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     (#) Configure the DMA controller to transfer the input data from the 
 122:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          memory using DMA_Init() function. 
 123:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          The transfer length is the length of the message. 
 124:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          As message padding is not managed by the peripheral, the message 
 125:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          length must be an entire number of blocks. The data are transferred 
 126:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          in burst mode. The burst length is 4 words in the AES and 2 or 4 
 127:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          words in the DES/TDES. The DMA should be configured to set an 
 128:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          interrupt on transfer completion of the output data to indicate that 
 129:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          the processing is finished. 
 130:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          Refer to DMA peripheral driver for more details.  
 131:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
 132:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****      (#) Enable the cryptographic processor using CRYP_Cmd() function. 
 133:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          Enable the DMA requests CRYP_DMAReq_DataIN and CRYP_DMAReq_DataOUT 
 134:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          using CRYP_DMACmd() function.
 135:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
 136:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****      (#) All the transfers and processing are managed by the DMA and the 
 137:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          cryptographic processor. The DMA transfer complete interrupt indicates 
 138:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          that the processing is complete. Both FIFOs are normally empty and 
 139:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****          CRYP_FLAG_BUSY flag is reset.
 140:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   
 141:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****     @endverbatim
 142:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *
 143:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   ******************************************************************************
 144:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @attention
