 464:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** /** @defgroup CRYP_Group3 Context swapping functions
 465:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *  @brief   Context swapping functions
 466:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *
 467:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** @verbatim   
 468:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===============================================================================
 469:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****                       ##### Context swapping functions #####
 470:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 471:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] This section provides functions allowing to save and store CRYP Context
 472:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 473:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] It is possible to interrupt an encryption/ decryption/ key generation process 
 474:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       to perform another processing with a higher priority, and to complete the 
 475:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       interrupted process later on, when the higher-priority task is complete. To do 
 476:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       so, the context of the interrupted task must be saved from the CRYP registers 
 477:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       to memory, and then be restored from memory to the CRYP registers.
 478:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    
