 650:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** /** @defgroup CRYP_Group4 CRYP's DMA interface Configuration function
 651:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *  @brief   CRYP's DMA interface Configuration function 
 652:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *
 653:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** @verbatim   
 654:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===============================================================================
 655:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****              ##### CRYP's DMA interface Configuration function #####
 656:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 657:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] This section provides functions allowing to configure the DMA interface for 
 658:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       CRYP data input and output transfer.
 659:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    
 660:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] When the DMA mode is enabled (using the CRYP_DMACmd() function), data can be 
 661:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       transferred:
 662:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (+) From memory to the CRYP IN FIFO using the DMA peripheral by enabling 
 663:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        the CRYP_DMAReq_DataIN request.
 664:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (+) From the CRYP OUT FIFO to the memory using the DMA peripheral by enabling 
 665:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        the CRYP_DMAReq_DataOUT request.
 666:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 667:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** @endverbatim
 668:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @{
 669:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   */
 670:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 671:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** /**
 672:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @brief  Enables or disables the CRYP DMA interface.
 673:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @param  CRYP_DMAReq: specifies the CRYP DMA transfer request to be enabled or disabled.
 674:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *           This parameter can be any combination of the following values:
 675:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *            @arg CRYP_DMAReq_DataOUT: DMA for outgoing(Tx) data transfer
 676:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *            @arg CRYP_DMAReq_DataIN: DMA for incoming(Rx) data transfer
 677:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @param  NewState: new state of the selected CRYP DMA transfer request.
 678:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   *          This parameter can be: ENABLE or DISABLE.
 679:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @retval None
 680:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   */
 681:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** void CRYP_DMACmd(uint8_t CRYP_DMAReq, FunctionalState NewState)
