 702:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** /** @defgroup CRYP_Group5 Interrupts and flags management functions
 703:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *  @brief   Interrupts and flags management functions
 704:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *
 705:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** @verbatim   
 706:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===============================================================================
 707:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****               ##### Interrupts and flags management functions #####
 708:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 709:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  
 710:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] This section provides functions allowing to configure the CRYP Interrupts and 
 711:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       to get the status and Interrupts pending bits.
 712:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 713:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] The CRYP provides 2 Interrupts sources and 7 Flags:
 714:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 715:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *** Flags : ***
 716:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ===============
 717:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] 
 718:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_FLAG_IFEM :  Set when Input FIFO is empty. This Flag is cleared only
 719:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        by hardware.
 720:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       
 721:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_FLAG_IFNF :  Set when Input FIFO is not full. This Flag is cleared 
 722:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        only by hardware.
 723:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 724:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 725:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_FLAG_INRIS  : Set when Input FIFO Raw interrupt is pending it gives 
 726:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        the raw interrupt state prior to masking of the input FIFO service interrupt.
 727:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        This Flag is cleared only by hardware.
 728:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****      
 729:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_FLAG_OFNE   : Set when Output FIFO not empty. This Flag is cleared 
 730:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        only by hardware.
 731:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****         
 732:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_FLAG_OFFU   : Set when Output FIFO is full. This Flag is cleared only 
 733:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        by hardware.
 734:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****                            
 735:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_FLAG_OUTRIS : Set when Output FIFO Raw interrupt is pending it gives 
 736:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        the raw interrupt state prior to masking of the output FIFO service interrupt.
 737:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        This Flag is cleared only by hardware.
 738:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****                                
 739:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_FLAG_BUSY   : Set when the CRYP core is currently processing a block 
 740:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        of data or a key preparation (for AES decryption). This Flag is cleared 
 741:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        only by hardware. To clear it, the CRYP core must be disabled and the last
 742:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        processing has completed. 
 743:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 744:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *** Interrupts : ***
 745:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  ====================
 746:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..]
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc52A741.s 			page 34


 747:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_IT_INI   : The input FIFO service interrupt is asserted when there 
 748:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       are less than 4 words in the input FIFO. This interrupt is associated to 
 749:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       CRYP_FLAG_INRIS flag.
 750:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 751:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       -@- This interrupt is cleared by performing write operations to the input FIFO 
 752:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****           until it holds 4 or more words. The input FIFO service interrupt INMIS is 
 753:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****           enabled with the CRYP enable bit. Consequently, when CRYP is disabled, the 
 754:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****           INMIS signal is low even if the input FIFO is empty.
 755:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 756:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 757:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 758:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) CRYP_IT_OUTI  : The output FIFO service interrupt is asserted when there 
 759:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        is one or more (32-bit word) data items in the output FIFO. This interrupt 
 760:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        is associated to CRYP_FLAG_OUTRIS flag.
 761:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 762:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        -@- This interrupt is cleared by reading data from the output FIFO until there 
 763:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****            is no valid (32-bit) word left (that is, the interrupt follows the state 
 764:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****            of the OFNE (output FIFO not empty) flag).
 765:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 766:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  *** Managing the CRYP controller events : ***
 767:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  =============================================
 768:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****  [..] The user should identify which mode will be used in his application to manage 
 769:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****       the CRYP controller events: Polling mode or Interrupt mode.
 770:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 771:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) In the Polling Mode it is advised to use the following functions:
 772:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) CRYP_GetFlagStatus() : to check if flags events occur. 
 773:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 774:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        -@@- The CRYPT flags do not need to be cleared since they are cleared as 
 775:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****             soon as the associated event are reset.   
 776:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 777:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 778:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****    (#) In the Interrupt Mode it is advised to use the following functions:
 779:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) CRYP_ITConfig()       : to enable or disable the interrupt source.
 780:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        (++) CRYP_GetITStatus()    : to check if Interrupt occurs.
 781:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 782:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****        -@@- The CRYPT interrupts have no pending bits, the interrupt is cleared as 
 783:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****              soon as the associated event is reset. 
 784:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** 
 785:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c **** @endverbatim
 786:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   * @{
 787:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_cryp.c ****   */ 
